# Panchnama environment variables
#
# Sessions 0-8 (audit pipeline: inventory, crawl, analyze, review, publish)
# need none of these — that pipeline reads/writes only local files under
# data/ and is fully usable with an empty environment. These variables are
# for Session 9's citizen-experience database only.
#
# Copy to .env.local for local development:
#   cp .env.example .env.local
# .env.local is git-ignored (see .gitignore) — never commit real credentials.

# --- Used by this session (packages/database) -------------------------------

# Postgres connection string for local development, read by
# packages/database (Drizzle/postgres.js) and by drizzle-kit. Matches the
# docker-compose.yml defaults below; if you change POSTGRES_USER/PASSWORD/DB/
# PORT here, update DATABASE_URL to match (docker-compose.yml does not read
# DATABASE_URL itself — it reads the discrete POSTGRES_* vars below).
DATABASE_URL=postgres://panchnama:panchnama@localhost:5432/panchnama

# Discrete vars docker-compose.yml uses to configure the local Postgres
# container. Safe local-dev defaults; change if 5432/panchnama/panchnama
# already conflict with something else on your machine.
POSTGRES_USER=panchnama
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=panchnama
POSTGRES_DB=panchnama
POSTGRES_PORT=5432

# Dedicated database for packages/database's integration test suite —
# separate from DATABASE_URL per implementation.md section 9.5's "separate
# local, test, preview, and production databases". Point this at a
# different database name (or a different local Postgres instance/port)
# than DATABASE_URL. See packages/database/README.md for how to create it.
TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://panchnama:panchnama@localhost:5432/panchnama_test

# Overrides for the retention policy in implementation.md section 9.8.
# Defaults (90 days / 24 hours) apply if unset — see
# packages/database/src/constants.ts.
# EXPERIENCE_RETENTION_REJECTED_DAYS=90
# EXPERIENCE_ABUSE_KEY_TTL_HOURS=24

# --- Reserved for Session 10, unused by any code in this session -----------

# HMAC secret Session 10's rate limiter will use to turn a request IP into
# the keyed hash stored in experience_abuse_keys, per implementation.md
# section 9.6/5.12's ban on storing raw IP addresses. No code in
# packages/database reads this yet — it is declared here now purely to
# establish the variable name before it has a consumer.
# EXPERIENCE_ABUSE_KEY_SECRET=
